  "note": "The seller client sends through the pinned connector to a public HTTPS origin and nothing else: it has no loopback, plain HTTP or fetch path and takes no unlisted option. The exact response bytes the connector read go to the wire's verification before any status is trusted; a redirect, an oversized answer, a stalled answer and a lost connection keep their own causes, and failureDispatched is false only when no request byte of any call was written. Each call can hand the effect boundary's two transmit callbacks to the connector unchanged, and no option or named method accepts them. The Agreement flows build the client over a connector made once per protocol object. createPublicSellerClient exposes the named POST methods under the admission wrapper, with the real connector and no durable request records."
